content:
Analysis of solvent selectivity for the separation of **Polyethylene (PE)** and **Ethylene Vinyl Alcohol (EVOH)** at **120 °C** identifies the following top candidates. In accordance with atmospheric pressure constraints, only solvents with a boiling point above 120 °C at 1 atm are ranked as viable candidates for operation at this temperature.

For the purposes of this analysis, **LDPE** is used as the representative polymer for PE.

### 1. Target: PE (LDPE) (Rejecting EVOH) at 120 °C
The following solvents provide the highest selectivity for dissolving Polyethylene while leaving EVOH solid at 120 °C.

| Rank | Solvent | Selectivity | PE Solubility (%) | EVOH Solubility (%) | BP (°C) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 1 | **Dodecane** | 32.93 | 32.97% | 0.04% | 216.2 |
| 2 | **1,4-Dimethylbenzene** (p-Xylene) | 32.61 | 33.17% | 0.56% | 138.4 |
| 3 | **1,2-Dimethylbenzene** (o-Xylene) | 31.74 | 32.34% | 0.60% | 144.4 |

*Note: High-selectivity solvents like cyclohexane, hexane, and toluene are excluded from this ranking as they would exceed their boiling points at the 120 °C target temperature.*

### 2. Target: EVOH (Rejecting PE/LDPE) at 120 °C
The following solvents provide the highest selectivity for dissolving EVOH while leaving Polyethylene solid at 120 °C.

| Rank | Solvent | Selectivity | EVOH Solubility (%) | PE Solubility (%) | BP (°C) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 1 | **Dimethyl sulfoxide** | 30.13 | 35.43% | 5.30% | 189.0 |
| 2 | **Dimethylformamide** | 12.97 | 30.72% | 17.75% | 153.0 |
| 3 | **Ethylene glycol** | 9.07 | 9.95% | 0.88% | 197.3 |

